# NOTICE

This skill's text is original. It was written from two books and informed by
public material; no third-party prose or code was copied.

## Books whose principles are distilled here

- Steven D. Katz, *Film Directing: Shot by Shot — Visualizing from Concept to Screen*,
  Michael Wiese Productions, 1991.
- Marcos Mateu-Mestre, *Framed Ink: Drawing and Composition for Visual Storytellers*,
  Design Studio Press, 2010.
- Bruce Block, *The Visual Story* (3rd ed., 2020) — referenced for the six
  structural variables in `composition.md`.
- Walter Murch, *In the Blink of an Eye* (2nd ed., 2001) — the Rule of Six
  priority order in `sequence-rhythm.md`; the weights are his published figures,
  the wording and the checks are ours.

No passages are reproduced; the page and chapter anchors in `references/sources.md`
exist so a reader can go back to the originals.

## Public material that informed structure (not copied)

- [62656456/ai-film-skills](https://github.com/62656456/ai-film-skills) (Apache-2.0):
  the idea of an indexed camera-mechanism library and a viewing-plan comparison
  before camera choice.
- [smixs/visual-skills](https://github.com/smixs/visual-skills) (CC BY 4.0,
  © Serge Shima): dramaturgy-first prompting, and the reminder that shot cards
  need physical facts rather than adjectives.
- [OpenAI Cookbook — Sora 2 Prompting Guide](https://github.com/openai/openai-cookbook/tree/main/examples/sora):
  one camera move plus one action per shot, actions written as beats and counts.
- [BytePlus Dreamina Seedance 2.5 prompt guide](https://docs.byteplus.com/zh-CN/docs/ModelArk/seedance-2-5-prompt-guide):
  duration and stage budgets used in `handoff.md`.

The mechanism IDs, beat taxonomy, dial system, storyboard overlay format and the
validators are original structures.

## Software

- Python 3 standard library.
- [Pillow](https://python-pillow.org/) for storyboard annotation.
- [FFmpeg](https://ffmpeg.org/) for animatic assembly (called as an external
  binary, not bundled).

## Artwork

Example panels were generated for this repository with NovelAI and are not
derived from the books.
